+### Optional same-owner renewal schema preparation
+
+A v3 renewal may perform one document-only read after the original worker-role/name checks and before revocation processing. An ambient actual Spring transaction disables preparation before this read. The detached, closed Jackson snapshot must pass the complete original session schema and the independently pinned expanded schema must expose the same compiled full OWNER child. This adds pre-revocation database/schema TRACE observations, copying and potentially earlier Error propagation; optional RuntimeException failure retains the original locked path. It creates no authority, persisted proof, cache, accounting mutation or new transaction.
+
+Actual claim guards and queries remain fresh and ordered. Only a same-owner live renewal with exact complete node-class, JSON and serialized representation agreement before lease mutation can use the call-local proof. At the original save validation point, the only permitted change is leaseExpiresAt; whole-session canonicalization remains fresh and the same compiled OWNER object validator checks all owner fields. Null, foreign, changed, unsupported or unavailable proof uses original public whole-schema save validation. The child entry has different internal root/path/TRACE context; only the original status-only INVALID_CONTRACT refusal is retained, with no rooted diagnostic equivalence claim. Resource changes require a new Contracts instance and any expanded fingerprint mismatch disables preparation.
+
+Original revocation/auth/source/assignment/fence/lease clipping/idempotency/atomic command writes and rollback stay unchanged. The additional read, full detached validation, representation comparisons and fallback cost may outweigh one removed locked traversal. Secret renewal 1000ms, revocation 2000ms, full ROOT+APP capture and privacy scans remain unchanged; this is not a latency, cause or acceptance claim. Existing sampler debug-line mappings become historical after these source edits.
